  <div class="tp-answer" id="quick-answer"><p><strong>Quick answer:</strong> the average waist size for men in the U.S. is <strong>40.6&nbsp;inches (103&nbsp;cm)</strong>, measured at the top of the hip bone (NHANES 2021&ndash;2023, men 20+). For health, keep it under <strong>40&nbsp;in (102&nbsp;cm)</strong>, ideally under 37&nbsp;in, and under half your height.</p></div>

  <nav class="pg-toc pg-toc--rows" id="page-contents" aria-label="Inside this waist size guide">
